+------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

| GIT COMMAND                        | EXPLANATION / DESCRIPTION                                               |
+------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

| git init                           | Initializes a brand new, empty local Git repository (.git folder).      |
| git clone <url>                    | Downloads an entire existing repository from GitHub to your desktop.    |
| Fork (GitHub Web Concept)          | A personal, independent copy of a repository hosted on your GitHub.     |
| git remote add origin <url>        | Links your local directory to a remote server address on GitHub.        |
| git remote -v                      | Lists all configured remote connection paths and internet URLs.         |
+------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

| git branch                         | Lists local branches. The active branch is marked with an asterisk (*). |
| git branch <branch-name>           | Creates a new branch timeline off your current line of code.            |
| git checkout <branch-name>         | Switches your active working workspace to a different branch.           |
| git checkout -b <branch-name>      | Shortcut command that creates a new branch and instantly switches to it. |
| git switch <branch-name>           | Modern, dedicated tool designed for switching between branches safely.  |
| git switch -c <branch-name>        | Modern shortcut that creates a brand new branch and switches to it.     |
+------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

| git fetch                          | Downloads history and tracking metadata from GitHub without merging it. |
| git merge <branch-name>            | Combines the history of a target branch directly into your active one.  |
| git pull                           | Fetches updates from GitHub and immediately runs a local history merge.  |
| git push                           | Uploads all locally saved and committed snapshots up to GitHub.         |
+------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

| git status                         | Shows the working directory status (untracked, modified, staged files).  |
| git show                           | Logs out detailed metadata and line expansions for the latest commit.   |
| git show <commit-hash>             | Inspects a specific historical commit to show exact line modifications. |
| git diff                           | Shows line-by-line differences between your files and last save state.  |
| git log                            | Displays a chronological history stream of all commits in this branch.   |
+------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

| git add .                          | Stages all current changes and untracked files for the next snapshot.   |
| git commit -m "message"            | Saves your staged changes locally with a descriptive comment message.   |
| git mv <source> <destination>      | Moves or renames a file path, staging the change automatically.         |
| git restore <file>                 | Discards unstaged file edits, rolling back to the last clean commit.    |
+------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
